fact WorkItem(id: "WI-772", description: some(value: "smt-gen mishandles bodied rules twice, surfaced by the WI-770 review. (a) lookup_explicit_policy (rustland/anthill-smt-gen/src/policy.rs:69) does `if !kb.is_fact(rid) { continue; }` -- a SILENT skip: a guarded `rule TranslationPolicy(...) :- <guard>` never applies even when its guard holds, and policy_for falls back to the Inline/LiftedAxiom defaults with no diagnostic -- the opposite polarity of WI-770's loud refusal for the identical authoring shape (repo rule: loud error over silent skip; the author gets no hint their rule shape is unsupported). (b) collect_facts_for_referenced_entities (rustland/anthill-smt-gen/src/lib.rs:1535) walks rules_by_functor with NO is_fact guard and accepts the first candidate whose head named_args carry concrete numeric literals: a bodied `rule LinkParameters(mass: 2.0, ...) :- heavy_variant()` feeds mass=2.0 into the SMT encoding whether or not the guard holds, so a formal safety proof can be discharged from a premise the source guarded -- an unsound 'proof passes' with no diagnostic, the highest-stakes instance of the class anywhere in the workspace. FIX DIRECTION: loud refusal (WI-770 shape) at both sites -- (a)'s message should name the rule and state that guarded policies are unsupported; (b) additionally keep refusing even when OTHER ground facts exist for the entity (the bodied rule may shadow or race the fact in enumeration order). Route through the WI-773 facts-only accessor if it lands first. ACCEPTANCE: a bodied TranslationPolicy rule and a bodied referenced-entity rule are each refused loudly in tests, never silently skipped or harvested; cargo-test green via scripts/test.sh."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: nil), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-07-19T13:08:07Z"))
